Testing that icmp_interface emits nft the kernel will accept for BOTH families.

IPv6 headers have no 'protocol' field -- it is 'nexthdr' -- and the IPv6 ICMP
protocol is 'icmpv6', not 'icmp'. pbr emitted 'ip6 protocol icmp', which nft
rejects:

  /var/run/pbr.nft:32:34-41: Error: syntax error, unexpected string
  add rule inet fw4 pbr_output ip6 protocol icmp counter goto pbr_mark_0x020000

and because the whole file is validated in one pass, setting 'Default ICMP
Interface' in LuCI stopped the service from starting and took every policy with
it. Reproduced on 1.2.3-r95 hardware; measured against nftables 1.1.6, where
'ip protocol icmp' and 'ip6 nexthdr icmpv6' are accepted and 'ip6 protocol icmp'
is not.

The ipv6_enabled guard was never the problem and is left alone: the rule was
already gated on it, it was simply malformed.

